    surface is already smooth everywhere in between.If you have a cubic or higher degree surface, asking for the maximal
    smoothness will give you tangent, curvature, etc. up to the degree-1
    continuity.  Asking for tangent will just give you tangent continuity.It should be mentioned that this is "C", not "G" continuity we're
    talking about, so technically, you can still see visual tangent breaks
    if the surface is degenerate.Note: A single smoothTangentSurface command cannot smooth in both directions
    at once; you must use two separate commands to do this.
    Args:
